## Scope and release
This first trial asks whether a genuinely new session can read a declared historical snapshot, identify its gaps/conflicts and propose one safe next action. Passing does not establish recovery of all current work, settle D1, replace Prime or release execution. The full continuity milestone still needs an authoritative current-work arrangement and an observed bounded task. Director must launch/name the actual fresh session; no identity is invented by compute or this review. Before that launch, retain a new prepared attempt, confirm no required omissions, provide the short purpose/environment/reading brief, and keep the evaluator out of candidate inputs. No model is called here.

## Avoid another open-ended build
Neither accepted return needs another implementation pack as a condition of accepting its declared scope. Next work is one final prepared test bundle and Director-led trial, with schema ambiguities resolved above. If preparation exposes a concrete defect, preserve it and fix that defect; do not weaken the passing rule or rewrite old evidence.
